{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt explicit linked request supersession for rejected implementation rounds. When an implementation artifact has a ratified changes-requested verdict and the requester moves the required repair into a child request, the old commitment closes only through an explicit supersession of the old request that also cites that exact successor request. Project this terminal state as superseded, with successor_request naming the child; do not call it satisfied, cancelled, or reneged. The supersession text records why substance moved. Admit the linked form only when: the target is an effective request with a reporting artifact; a ratified changes-requested verdict names that artifact exact head; exactly one effective successor request is cited after the target; that child directly rests on the target; and the child requester is the target requester. Existing supersession authority remains unchanged: only the request author or a ratifier may file it. An ordinary request retirement without a qualifying successor keeps current withdrawn or cancelled meaning. Later retirement or failure of the child does not rewrite the historical transfer; the child row records that outcome. Add successor_request to the projection and treat superseded as terminal. Advance the Workroom fold profile because replayed projection bytes and lifecycle meaning change. After deployment, file one linked supersession per audited stuck parent to its canonical repair child; that explicit migration drains the nine rows. This remains preferred over ratifying a rejected artifact, which would conflate acceptance with transfer and provide no successor pointer, and over inferring from any child request, which would silently close additive follow-up work. This replaces stale proposal 7147120f without changing its design."}